  data: {
    LLM: "Learn the standard Pai Gow tile ranking system. Set your hands according to the house way (standard optimal splitting). The side bets are independent decisions â€” the Bonus bet has moderate hit frequency, the Tie bet capitalises on the high push rate.\n\nIn standard Pai Gow, the house edge is significantly reduced when players take turns banking. However, Bonanza Pai Gow's Bonus and Tie bets have FIXED house edges regardless of who banks â€” making them purely house-advantage bets.\n\nOptimal main-bet strategy: bank whenever possible (standard Pai Gow advice). Side-bet strategy: the Bonus bet's ~27% hit rate (every 3.7 hands) provides frequent wins with moderate variance. The Tie bet exploits the ~40% push rate but typically has a higher house edge. Calculate expected value for each bet independently.",
